{
  "id": 97859851,
  "iid": 2854,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "Don't cast away upper bits when assigning to a nstime_t's secs field.",
  "description": "The secs field is a time_t, which is not necessarily 32 bits.  If it's\nnot, casting away the upper bits, by casting to guint32, introduces a\nY2.038K bug.\n\nEither cast to time_t or, if you're assigning a time_t to it, don't\nbother with the cast.",
  "state": "merged",
